# trackB_train_fullscale.summary.log
# Track B - full-scale GBT training, 6 Sep 2026. 300 trees, 241 cities.
# Distilled from trackB_train_fullscale.log (121,083 lines, 13.4 MB) by
# removing MemoryStore/BlockManager cache-eviction warnings and stack frames.
#
# HOW TO READ THE ERROR-LOOKING LINES IN THE MIDDLE
#   "Connection reset by peer", "Broken pipe", "EofException", and the
#   glassfish/jersey MappableException blocks are NOT training failures. They
#   were produced by an external monitor polling the Spark UI REST API
#   (localhost:4040/api/v1/applications/.../jobs) every few minutes to
#   estimate progress; each closed HTTP connection made Spark's embedded
#   Jetty log an EOF. They coincide with the polling timestamps and stop when
#   polling stopped.
#
#   The two "Bad response ERROR ... from datanode" lines are transient HDFS
#   read errors on a 4-node cluster under memory pressure. Spark retried the
#   affected tasks; the run continued and finished with PASS.
#
#   The evidence that matters is the PHASE 6 - EVALUATION block at the end.
# ==========================================================================

